  "result": "Fixed. `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound could return a value outside the range; it now returns the nearest value that is inside it.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py` returned `bound - dir` for open bounds. `dir` is the direction back into the range, so the sign was backwards. With `IntRange(0, 5, clamp=True, min_open=True)`, the input `-1` returned `-1`, which is not greater than 0. With `max_open=True`, the input `10` returned `6`, which is not less than 5.\n\n**Change:** `_clamp` now returns `bound + dir`, so `min_open` clamps to `min + 1` and `max_open` clamps to `max - 1`.\n\n**Tests:** I added four cases to `tests/test_types.py` covering both bounds, including the boundary value itself. `tests/test_types.py` and `tests/test_info_dict.py` pass (73 passed, 2 skipped). I did not run the full suite.\n\nI did not commit anything.",
